::SPEECH_U05_L07_Quiz_Q01::
Question ID: SPEECH_U05_L07_Quiz_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.DIG.01
Question:
Online collaborative publication item 1: Which choice best prepares a digital speech product for audience-ready publication?
{
~A. Publish the first draft without reviewing it#This choice is incomplete because it does not support clear publication, revision, audience awareness, or digital presentation quality.
=B. Assign revision roles and check the final version for clarity#Correct. This choice supports publication-ready communication by improving clarity, collaboration, digital presentation, and audience understanding.
~C. Ignore audience needs during final review#This choice reflects a misconception. Recheck revision, publication readiness, audience impact, or slide coherence.
~D. Let everyone edit without roles or version control#This choice weakens the communication product because it ignores how the audience will use or understand it.
}
::SPEECH_U05_L07_Quiz_Q02::
Question ID: SPEECH_U05_L07_Quiz_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.COM.03
Question:
Online collaborative publication item 2: Which choice best prepares a digital speech product for audience-ready publication?
{
~A. Publish the first draft without reviewing it#This choice is incomplete because it does not support clear publication, revision, audience awareness, or digital presentation quality.
~B. Add more decoration instead of improving meaning#This choice may sound related, but it does not fully meet the communication purpose or collaboration standard.
~C. Ignore audience needs during final review#This choice reflects a misconception. Recheck revision, publication readiness, audience impact, or slide coherence.
=D. Use version control so the group submits the current draft#Correct. This choice supports publication-ready communication by improving clarity, collaboration, digital presentation, and audience understanding.
}
